From 13147defe251563609b21ecb77641036325acfc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:58:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): make a remote-links memo miss read and
 re-project only changed replica rows [daveey]

hermes-hub's replica (~12.7k task rows, 56 MB JSON) changes every ~30 s, so the
remote-links memo missed constantly and each miss re-read, re-decoded and
re-projected every row under _links_lock (41 thread-seconds of lock wait per
90 s on the always-on dashboard after round 1).

kanban_replica_rows keeps the rows keyed by (gw, key) and on a miss fetches only
rows with seq above the last seen, in one aggregated statement; the probe totals
(count, seq, version, data length) prove deletes and catch in-place rewrites.
kanban_replica_projection keeps each row's clock-free projection and rebuilds
only the aggregates when hub staleness or an owner scope's freshness flips. A
replica without seq/version, a row without seq, a replaced file or any
unexplained total falls back to the full read. Both paths now emit rows in
(gw, key) order; a 12k-row fixture compares them step by step.
